{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"partition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"by"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/MutableCollection\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:SM7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Bool","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/MutableCollection\/Index","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SM5IndexQa"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"belongsInSecondPartition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A predicate used to partition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the collection. All elements satisfying this predicate are ordered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after all elements not satisfying it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The index of the first element in the reordered collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that matches "},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If no elements in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection match "},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the returned index is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to the collection’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After partitioning a collection, there is a pivot index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no element before "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"predicate and every element at or after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"type":"text","text":". This operation isn’t guaranteed to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable, so the relative ordering of elements within the partitions might"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the following example, an array of numbers is partitioned by a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"predicate that matches elements greater than 30."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers = [30, 40, 20, 30, 30, 60, 10]","let p = numbers.partition(by: { $0 > 30 })","\/\/ p == 5","\/\/ numbers == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30, 60, 40]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numbers"},{"type":"text","text":" array is now arranged in two partitions. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numbers[..<p]"},{"type":"text","text":", is made up of the elements that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not greater than 30. The second partition, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numbers[p...]"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is made up of the elements that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"are"}]},{"type":"text","text":" greater than 30."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let first = numbers[..<p]","\/\/ first == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30]","let second = numbers[p...]","\/\/ second == [60, 40]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that the order of elements in both partitions changed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That is, "},{"code":"40","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" appears before "},{"code":"60","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the original collection,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but, after calling "},{"code":"partition(by:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"60"},{"type":"text","text":" appears before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"40"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of the collection."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EmptyCollection\/partition(by:)-37csa","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"Swift","externalID":"s:SMsE9partition2by5IndexQzSb7ElementQzKXE_tKF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s15EmptyCollectionV","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"d